@startuml
title FST-051 - Select installed applications
actor User
participant "Distractions UI" as UI
participant "Local API" as API
participant "Application catalog" as Catalog
participant "Native metadata" as OS
participant "Foreground monitor" as Monitor
participant "Blocking policy" as Policy
database "Local database" as DB
User -> UI: Add distraction / Application
UI -> API: GET /api/v1/applications
API -> Catalog: discover or use 60-second cache
Catalog -> OS: read native and package metadata
OS --> Catalog: applications and provider warnings
Catalog --> API: typed targets and availability
API --> UI: catalog for current platform
UI --> User: searchable checkboxes / manual fallback
User -> UI: select apps and add
UI -> API: POST /api/v1/blocking-rules/batch
API -> Policy: validate all / lock policy once
alt invalid or duplicate target
  Policy --> API: reject complete batch
  API --> UI: 422 / 409; no partial additions
  UI --> User: preserve selection and show error
else valid batch
  Policy -> DB: save all rules in one transaction
  DB --> Policy: committed rules
  Policy --> API: saved DTOs
  API --> UI: 201 and saved rules
end
== During an eligible focus interval ==
Monitor -> OS: resolve actual foreground process identity
OS --> Monitor: PID / start time / executable / optional app ID
Monitor -> Policy: evaluate exact identity
note right of Policy
Path > app ID > process name.
Never target a shared package launcher.
Existing suspension/recovery safeguards apply.
end note
@enduml
